.TH MECHLAB 2
.SH NAME
mechlab: run, parse \- Danby mechanism models as scripts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "sys.m";
include "draw.m";
include "mechlab.m";
mechlab := load Mechlab Mechlab->PATH;

err := mechlab->run(ctxt, name, spec);
(m, links, err) := mechlab->parse(spec);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Mechlab
is the Danby mechanism viewer as a library the model calls, driven by a
script.  A model is one file: its equations, its parameters, its
geometry and an
.B init()
that says
.PP
.EX
mechlab->run(ctxt, "slidingpendulum1", SPEC);
.EE
.PP
.B Run
parses
.IR spec ,
opens a window titled by it, and integrates and draws until the user
closes the window.  It returns nil, or a string naming what is wrong
with the spec; a caller should raise on that rather than open a window
that cannot work.
.PP
The vocabulary is
.IR dynsys (2)'s
\(em
.BR param ,
.BR maxtime ,
.BR state ,
.BR derivative ,
.BR eq ,
.B observable
and
.B point
\(em plus three lines of this library's own:
.TP
.BI title " text..."
The window title and status line.  Required.
.TP
.BI manual " page"
The
.IR wmman (1)
page behind the window's own help button.  Defaults to
.BI danby- name\fR,\fP
the name passed to
.BR run() .
.TP
.BI link " name name"
Draw a rod between two
.BR point s.
Repeatable.  The points are named rather than numbered, so that
inserting a point above does not silently renumber the links below it.
.PP
Exactly two
.B observable
lines are required \(em they are the two traces on the graph \(em and at
least one
.BR point .
.PP
.B Parse
is the spec alone, with no window: the test seam.  It returns the model
and the link table, or nil and an error string.
.IR Mechlabtest (1)
checks a model's own numbers through it without a display.
.PP
A model file includes
.BR sys.m ,
then
.BR draw.m ,
then
.BR mechlab.m ,
and nothing else: this module includes
.B dynsys.m
(and so
.BR hoc.m )
itself, so a model need not know they exist.  Limbo has no include
guard, so a caller that has already included
.B dynsys.m
must not include this one.
.PP
The window is Tk's.  The parameter sliders are Tk scales, the buttons are
Tk buttons, the status line is a Tk label, and the layout is a Tk
geometry manager's; the mechanism and the graph are two
.IR panel (9)
widgets holding images the library draws into, the same arrangement
.IR coffee (1)
uses for its animation.  Draw is used for the pixels of those two
pictures and for nothing else, which is where it is genuinely better than
a widget tree \(em a phase portrait redrawn forty times a second is not a
canvas item.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/mechlab.b
